When we expand $(a+b)^n = (a+b)(a+b) dots.c(a+b)$, we obtain terms of the form $a^(n-k)b^k$ where $0 <= k <= n$. The number of terms of the form $a^(n-k) b^k$ in the expansion is $binom(n, k)$, since we must specify $k$ brackets from which to pick $b$. Hence
$ (a+b)^n = sum_(k=0)^n binom(n, k) a^(n-k) b^k. $
